---
layout: layouts/base.njk
pagination:
  data: directory.categories
  size: 1
  alias: cat
permalink: "/directory/{{ cat.slug }}/"
eleventyComputed:
  title: "{{ cat.label }} · Largs"
  heading: "{{ cat.label }}"
  subtitle: "{{ cat.blurb }}"
---
{# One page per directory category, same shape as the council register:
   Eleventy renders this template once per entry in directory.categories
   and permalink writes each to its own folder. Real HTML pages —
   bookmarkable, indexable, back-button correct, working with JavaScript
   off. The chips on the front page are plain links to these.

   TWO CATEGORY STATES. A category with `open: true` has no listings and
   says so, inviting them. That is deliberate for food, trades and
   accommodation: a partial list of businesses competing for the same
   customer reads as a recommendation, and this site takes no view on
   named businesses. Those categories get populated only when the list is
   genuinely complete, or not at all.

   EVERY page carries the "who is missing" line, not only the empty ones.
   The populated categories are the likeliest to prompt a correction —
   somebody who runs a group will notice it is absent and say so, which
   is how the gaps get filled. #}

<section class="wrap council-page" aria-labelledby="page-title">
  <div class="rule" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  {% if cat.open %}
  <p class="page-intro">There are no listings here yet, and rather than
  publish a handful we would rather wait until the list is worth trusting.
  A few names out of many reads as a recommendation, and this site does not
  make recommendations about local businesses.</p>

  <h2>Get listed</h2>
  <p>Listings are free, and always will be. There is no charge to appear, no
  charge to stay, and no way to pay for a better position — everything is
  listed alphabetically.</p>
  <p>Send the following to
  <a href="mailto:hello@largs.scot?subject=Directory%20listing">hello@largs.scot</a>:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>The name of the business</li>
    <li>What it does, in a sentence</li>
    <li>Where it is, or the area it covers</li>
    <li>A phone number, a website, or both</li>
  </ul>
  <p>That is all. We will check the details are current before adding
  anything, and we will not publish anything else about you.</p>

  {% else %}
  <p class="page-intro">{{ cat.blurb }} Listed alphabetically — this is not
  a ranking, and nothing here is a recommendation.</p>

  <div class="directory-list">
    {% for item in cat.entries %}
    <div class="directory-item">
      <h2 class="directory-name">
        {% if item.url %}<a href="{{ item.url }}" rel="noopener">{{ item.name }}</a>{% else %}{{ item.name }}{% endif %}
      </h2>
      {% if item.blurb %}<p>{{ item.blurb }}</p>{% endif %}
      {% if item.where or item.phone %}
      <p class="directory-meta">
        {%- if item.where %}{{ item.where }}{% endif -%}
        {%- if item.where and item.phone %} · {% endif -%}
        {%- if item.phone %}<a href="tel:{{ item.phone | replace(" ", "") }}">{{ item.phone }}</a>{% endif -%}
      </p>
      {% endif %}
      {% if item.note %}<p class="directory-note">{{ item.note }}</p>{% endif %}
      <p class="directory-checked">Checked {{ item.checked }}</p>
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
  {% endif %}

  <div class="rule" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <h2>Who have we missed?</h2>
  <p>This list is built by hand and it will be incomplete. If something is
  missing, closed, moved, or wrong, please tell us —
  <a href="mailto:hello@largs.scot?subject=Directory%20—%20{{ cat.label }}">hello@largs.scot</a>.
  Listings are free and there is nothing to pay, ever.</p>
</section>
